Version 0.4.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-05

Cassini is now called Cassini talk. Your Library stays in Music/Cassini.

- Recording starts reliably when the computer is silent: the other people's
  side waits for the first sound instead of failing the start
- When a microphone or the computer's sound cannot open, Cassini says why and
  keeps recording what did open; if nothing opened, no empty meeting is left
  behind. Quit no longer waits for a microphone that never delivers audio
- Silent sources are saved as exact silence, so writing down and speaker
  separation skip them instead of reading noise
- Every part of Cassini places each track at the same start, so playback,
  transcripts and speakers line up; words stay inside the time a person was
  present, and a turn never spans a gap. Cassini for Mac passes the same check
- Browser meetings: set up the companion from Cassini, connect in the
  background, keep recording through page reloads, record automatically only
  once a call has really started, and record with no window open. Browser and
  computer audio share one clock, even when the system clock is adjusted
  during a meeting. The companion is now version 0.2.13: a long silent stretch
  no longer slows a browser recording's clock
- GNOME and Mac pass the same end-to-end tests: a recording followed live
  while it is in progress (shared test 2), and the same three outcome files
  (shared test 8)
- While recording: a live spectrogram for each side, Recording details that
  show what is being captured, a warning when muted output would silence the
  computer's sound, and a test recording to check your setup
- Library: move meetings to Trash with five seconds to undo, rename with F2,
  and keep each saved meeting as a portable Cassini file
- Writing down shows its progress before the first words, reads a track again
  without voice detection when it finds too few words there, and names the app
  version when it downloads models
- Translated into Italian, French, Spanish and Portuguese (Brazil and Portugal)
- Many capture fixes: interrupted and re-anchored inputs, frozen browser
  connections, and a live spectrum that no longer stops after the window
  stalls

Version 0.3.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-29

- Reconnect the browser companion with Connect in Cassini after updating.
  Native host identifiers now use io.codemyriad; do not rerun install-host.py
  with an old extension ID
- Keep recordings and received meetings in the Library, play their transcripts,
  search across meetings, and import or export audio and transcripts
- Record browser meetings independently, with a microphone choice for each one;
  optionally record meetings automatically while the window is closed
- Choose What is recorded during a meeting; keep recording this computer's sound
  if the browser connection is lost
- Set up the browser companion from Cassini, including in the Flatpak
- Write meetings down locally with bundled Whistle, or download the optional
  Parakeet Ultra model; the packages include both engines on x86_64
- Tell speakers apart with an optional model, name or clear their names, merge
  speakers and undo merges
- Remember saved voices locally, recognise them in new meetings, play samples,
  and forget individual voices or everyone
- Keep audio aligned when an input is interrupted, without adding silence for
  gradual device-clock drift

Version 0.2.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-27

- Record meetings: microphone and desktop audio into an Opus file
- Record browser meetings source by source with the companion extension for
  Chromium-based browsers; its native messaging hosts are registered per user
- Optionally record every browser meeting automatically, with a Stop notification
- Name missing libraries and GStreamer plugins at startup
- Packages for Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora, openSUSE, Arch Linux and Alpine, built and
  tested with the same scripts locally and in CI

Version 0.1.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

- Fix transcript-click crashes and GTK label sizing warnings
- Keep participants visible and rejoin interrupted speech with inline interjections
- Preserve interjections in exports

Version 0.1.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

First release.

- Play Cassini portable meetings with a transcript that follows playback
- Click words and timestamps to seek
- Speaker filter, transcript chooser, search
- Summary view with action items and topics
- Audio integrity check (exact-opus-audio-v1)
- Export as text or WebVTT
